WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.709
Joe Biden says that he would not legalize
cannabis because it is a supposedly gateway

00:00:06.709 --> 00:00:07.709
drug.

00:00:07.709 --> 00:00:14.310
So this is a very good opportunity to dispel
what is a very tired and misunderstood talking

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:15.310
point.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:19.820
And it's another confirmation, not that we
needed one, that Joe Biden's not progressive

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:20.820
period.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:27.859
Joe Biden's still has some of the tired, centrist
ideas of many decades past.

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:32.349
So let's take a look at the video from Joe
Biden's rally in Las Vegas, Nevada over the

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:33.370
weekend.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.860
And then, I mean, there's just so much to
say about this.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.270
Uh, my name is Ricky.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.870
Um, I have two questions show.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:44.199
Um, my first question is, has your stance
on recreational marijuana changed?

00:00:44.199 --> 00:00:52.210
And my second question is, do you mind signing
a poster for me in the moment?

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.449
I'd be happy to sign the poster and no, it
hasn't changed.

00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:58.829
I think, look, I think States should be able
to make a judgment to legalize marijuana.

00:00:58.829 --> 00:00:59.829
I agree with.

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:03.899
I think that's okay, but let me tell you the
truth of the matter is we, there's not nearly

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:11.860
been enough evidence that has been, uh, acquired
as to whether or not it is a gateway drug.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:17.520
It's a debate and I want a lot more before
I legalize it nationally, I want to make sure

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.390
we know a lot more about the science behind
it.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:25.900
It is really important to break this down
into pieces and go through it as I like to

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:30.299
do step-by-step because there's a lot of wrong
information here, but we also don't want to

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:32.110
go further than the science tells us.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:37.219
We just want to be clear about what does the
science say and how do these things work.

00:01:37.219 --> 00:01:43.439
The concept of a gateway drug, the concept
described by the idea of a gateway drug is

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:44.439
a real thing.

00:01:44.439 --> 00:01:45.439
Okay.

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:51.619
The idea is you have a drug, it's either in
of itself, not addictive or less addictive,

00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:57.930
but it leads to the use of more addicting
or deliberate debilitating drugs that one

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:04.109
may not as readily get into directly were
it not through the gateway or the door that

00:02:04.109 --> 00:02:08.160
is opened by some other substance or drug.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.660
So I'll give you an example.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:16.910
Prescription opiate painkillers have been
proven to function as a potentially dangerous

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.120
gateway to street heroin.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.120
That's true.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.120
That's a huge problem.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.090
You get a prescription, uh, for, uh, after
some medical procedure or an accident from

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.160
a doctor.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.090
Um, you become addicted.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:34.940
You start buying the same pills on the street,
you realize heroin is cheaper.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:40.670
So you switched to the heroin, the prescription
opiates for so many people, uh, devastatingly

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:43.470
have been a gateway to street heroin.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.600
That's a real problem.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.650
Cannabis has not been shown to be a gateway
drug and there's actually a ton of science

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.650
about it.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.640
You can go to Google scholar and you can read
lots of studies about it.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.810
And the general findings after I reviewed
it, several dozen studies about this are that

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:06.130
there actually is a correlation between very
heavy cannabis use and the use of harder drugs,

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.360
but the problem is that that's deceptive and
that's as far as many people go.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.870
There are many people who will say, well look,
studies have shown that really heavy cannabis

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:18.120
users are more likely to also be users or
abusers of heavier drugs.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.180
There must be some causal relationship.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:25.450
This is a very different issue altogether
and we shouldn't conflate what's going on.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:32.970
A heavy cannabis user could be more likely
to get into harder drugs regardless of their

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.510
cannabis use and regardless of the legality
of cannabis.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:43.170
What I mean by that is if you are the type
of person who either for biological reasons

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:49.010
or circumstantial family environmental reasons
are more likely to end up using heroin or

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:55.810
cocaine and crystal meth or whatever, you
are also more likely to do that regardless

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.680
of whether cannabis is legal.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.909
I hope I'm being clear in what I'm saying
here.

00:03:59.909 --> 00:04:07.430
Now there is one way in which marijuana or
cannabis can be a gateway drug and it's actually

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.240
something that suggests we should be legalizing
it.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:16.140
Being around drug related violence, being
around drug related guns and criminality and

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:23.690
drug dealing that is happening in an illicit
way is going to put you in situations where

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:28.710
there are likely going to be users of heavier
drugs around you.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:34.550
You could get sucked into it or into violence
or criminality simply by being around the

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:35.550
scene.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:40.940
But that's actually an argument for the legalization
of cannabis to get people who choose to use

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:46.680
it away from situations and circumstances
where there are heavier drugs or there are

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.740
guns or there is violence.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:56.190
That is the way in which cannabis being illegal
can serve as a gateway, not just to using

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:00.660
hard drugs, but also to getting people into
situations of criminality and violence that

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.560
are generated by cannabis being illegal.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:08.380
So back to Joe Biden, it's no surprise that
this is what he's saying.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.500
He's being upfront and I disagree with his
position.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.770
So the one thing I, I'm not a Biden guy, but
this is yet more evidence that Biden's not

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:15.910
progressive.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:19.630
The one thing, I appreciate that Joe Biden
is doing this election cycle, and I've said

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.370
this before and some people get mad for, for
me pointing this out, but it's true.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:27.020
Joe Biden doesn't seem to be pretending to
be a progressive.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.010
In other words, he makes very clear on the
stage.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:33.250
He's not into this Medicare for all thing
that other people are talking about.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.740
He makes it very clear when he's asked.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:37.800
I think cannabis is a gateway drug and I wouldn't
legalize it.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:42.880
I disagree vehemently or as I like to save
a humanly, even though I, I don't even know

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:43.880
where I heard it.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:44.880
I just find it funny.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:50.750
I disagree vehemently with Joe Biden on these
positions, but he's not playing coy the way

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.540
some other candidates have been doing.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:57.470
And it makes it really clear that Biden's
not the guy for me, I don't have to dig too

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:59.180
deep to figure that out.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:03.790
So, um, he's not the person I want as the
progressive, uh, as the democratic nominee,

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:04.790
rather.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:07.260
He's not the person I want as president, but
he's being upfront with us.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:08.100
He's completely wrong, but he is being upfront
with us here.

